title: 'statement gossip: remove the per-peer known-statement cache'
doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    The statement gossip protocol kept an LRU cache of up to 4 Mi statement hashes
    (~320 MiB) per connected peer, which a peer could fill just by sending statements.
    Propagation now remembers, for one tick, the peers each statement was received
    from and skips them when sending, using no per-peer memory. A peer may receive a
    duplicate statement around an initial sync, a follow-up will remove these duplicates.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `MAX_KNOWN_STATEMENTS` is removed from `sc_network_statement::config`, and
    `Peer::new_for_testing` loses its known-statements parameter.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: major
